From 6768e5bcafa11777276073dd159d4fa2ec05adbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: p104-k1-builder <k1@z4-p104.local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:47:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] p104 k1 v10: replace v9 per-row clamp and in-kernel
 alignment fallback (both cost speed, 2..3 columns up to 2x slower)

- last block of a multi-row Pascal launch is shifted back to end at the last matrix row: no read past the tensor,
  shared rows recomputed bit-identically, no extra registers
- 16-byte alignment is asserted on the host for the wide path instead of a per-call branch
- keeps v9: small_k threshold restored, trace compiled out, __ldg loads, n=1..3 and small-K perf cases

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu | 89 +++++++++++++-------------------------
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
index b0522f4..3cf85f3 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu
